## 7. Exploitation — Unauthorized Invitation Acceptance

### 7.1 Identifying the acceptance endpoint

During API testing, I identified the following endpoint:

```http
POST /api/invites/INV-0004/accept
```

This endpoint handles invitation acceptance.

The application did not provide an acceptance action in the authenticated account's invitation management interface.

I therefore tested the acceptance endpoint directly using my existing authenticated session.

### 7.2 Exploitation request

```http
POST /api/invites/INV-0004/accept HTTP/1.1
Host: <lab-host>
Authorization: Bearer <redacted>
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: */*
```

The request was submitted without providing proof of ownership of the invitation's intended recipient email address.

### 7.3 Server response

```http
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
```

Response body:

```json
{
  "message": "Invite accepted successfully",
  "project_uuid": "proj-glob-data-plat-002",
  "project_name": "Data Platform",
  "role": "member"
}
```

### Observations

The server:

1. Processed the acceptance request using my authenticated session.
2. Accepted an invitation intended for `consultant@external.com`.
3. Returned a successful HTTP response.
4. Confirmed the Data Platform project.
5. Returned the assigned member role.

The application did not adequately enforce the relationship between the authenticated account and the intended invitation recipient.

