## 9. Attack Flow

1. Authenticate to the application using an existing user account.
2. Inspect the activity API for invitation-related records.
3. Identify invitation ID 4 associated with organization ID 2.
4. Retrieve the invitation through `GET /api/invites/INV-0004`.
5. Identify the intended recipient email and associated project.
6. Submit a POST request to the invitation acceptance endpoint using the authenticated session.
7. Observe the successful acceptance response.
8. Retrieve the invitation again and verify that its status changed to accepted.

### Evidence correlation

| Step | Endpoint | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Discovery | GET /api/activity | Invitation associated with org ID 2 identified |
| Enumeration | GET /api/invites/INV-0004 | External recipient and project details retrieved |
| Exploitation | POST /api/invites/INV-0004/accept | HTTP 200; acceptance successful |
| Verification | GET /api/invites/INV-0004 | Status confirmed as accepted |

