## 10. Security Impact

An authenticated attacker could potentially accept invitations intended for other users when the application fails to enforce recipient email ownership.

Potential consequences include:

### 10.1 Unauthorized project membership

An attacker may redeem an invitation intended for another individual and receive the role associated with that invitation.

### 10.2 Cross-organization authorization bypass

Missing recipient and organization authorization checks could allow authenticated users to accept invitations associated with projects outside their intended organizational boundary.

### 10.3 Unauthorized role assignment

The application may assign the invitation's predefined role to an unintended authenticated account.

The demonstrated invitation assigned the `member` role.

### 10.4 Potential exposure of organizational resources

If the accepted membership grants access to project resources, an attacker may gain access to project information, tasks, or other organizational data.

This additional impact requires separate verification.

